Let $\mathbf{M} = \begin{pmatrix} a & b \\ c & d \end{pmatrix}.$
Then,
\begin{align*}
\mathbf{M} \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix} &= \begin{pmatrix} a & b \\ c & d \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ 0 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 3a \\ 3c \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 6 \\ 21 \end{pmatrix},
\end{align*}so $3a = 6$ and $3c = 21$ (i.e. $a = 2$ and $c = 7.$) Therefore, $\mathbf{M} = \begin{pmatrix} 2 & b \\ 7 & d \end{pmatrix}.$
Similarly, \begin{align*}
\mathbf{M} \begin{pmatrix} -1 \\ 5 \end{pmatrix} &= \begin{pmatrix} 2 & b \\ 7 & d \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} -1 \\ 5 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} -2 + 5b \\ -7 + 5d \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 3 \\ -17 \end{pmatrix},
\end{align*}so $-2 + 5b = 3$ and $-7 + 5d = -17$ (i.e. $b = 1$ and $d = -2.$)
Thus, $\mathbf{M} = \boxed{\begin{pmatrix} 2 & 1 \\ 7 & -2 \end{pmatrix}}.$The answer is: \begin{pmatrix}2&1\7&-2\end{pmatrix}
